## 1. Purpose

The purpose of this License is to permit broad personal, educational, commercial, and professional use of the Software without requiring payment of a monetary licence fee. Optional paid Access Tiers do not change this purpose.

In exchange for the rights granted under this License, Licensees agree to provide public Attribution when distributing Outputs created using the Software.

The parties acknowledge and agree that Attribution constitutes the primary consideration received by the Licensor in exchange for granting rights under this License.

The Attribution Requirements are therefore an essential condition of this License and not merely a request, courtesy, or voluntary acknowledgment.

Licensees who need terms more permissive than this License may contact the Licensor through https://stravelakis.com/forge to request a separate licence under Section 8.

## 2. Definitions

**"Licensor"** means the individual or entity distributing the Software under this License.

**"Software"** means the Video Forge source code, object code, libraries, modules, templates, and documentation that the Licensor publishes under this License, and updates to them published under this License. The Software does not include Extra Content.

**"Extra Content"** means characters, voices, motions, media, templates, packs, and other materials that the Licensor delivers only after registration or Key validation, together with any Key, server, or online service operated by the Licensor.

**"Derivative Software"** means any modification, adaptation, fork, extension, port, derivative work, or redistributed version of the Software.

**"Licensee"** means any individual or entity exercising rights under this License. Where an individual accepts this License on behalf of a company, organisation, or other entity, "Licensee" includes that entity.

**"Output"** means any video, animation, motion graphic, audiovisual work, rendered media file, or similar content generated wholly or partially through use of the Software.

**"Public Distribution"** means any publication, upload, streaming, hosting, broadcasting, sale, licensing, exhibition, embedding, transmission, sharing, or making available of an Output to one or more third parties.

**"Attribution"** means a clear notice that Video Forge was used in creating the Output, together with a reference to https://stravelakis.com/forge.

**"Approved Attribution Method"** means any Attribution method published by the Licensor on https://stravelakis.com/forge or in the Software documentation.

**"Provenance Signal"** means any label, watermark, metadata entry, or other marker that the Software adds to an Output to show that it was made with Video Forge or with artificial intelligence.

**"Online Service"** means making the Software or Derivative Software available to third parties so that they can create Outputs without receiving a copy of the Software, whether through a website, application, application programming interface, or any other remote means, with or without charge.

**"Notice File"** means a plain text file named `NOTICE` distributed with the Software or Derivative Software.

**"Serious Misuse"** means any use prohibited by Section 13.

**"Key"** means an access credential issued by the Licensor to a registered person.

**"Access Tier"** means one of the levels of access described in Section 12.

**"Access Controls"** means the Key checks, usage limits, feature limits, and other technical measures by which the Software applies an Access Tier.

**"Tier Terms"** means the description of each Access Tier published by the Licensor on https://stravelakis.com/forge or in the Software documentation.

