## 11. Online Services

A Licensee may operate the Software or Derivative Software as an Online Service, including as a paid service, provided that:

- the Online Service prominently displays "Built with Video Forge - https://stravelakis.com/forge" in its user interface and on its website;
- every Output that the Online Service delivers to its users carries Attribution in a form that meets Sections 4 to 6, and the Online Service does not offer its users a way to remove it;
- the Online Service binds its users, by enforceable terms, to keep that Attribution when they Publicly Distribute those Outputs, and to restrictions at least as protective as Section 13;
- where Keys have been introduced under Section 12, the operator holds its own Key, at the Friend in Good Standing tier or higher, and the Access Tier of that Key applies to the Online Service.

Users of an Online Service who Publicly Distribute Outputs from it must keep the Attribution those Outputs carry.

An operator who wants to offer an Online Service without these conditions may request a separate licence under Section 8.

## 12. Access Tiers, Keys and Extra Content

**Registration, Keys and Access Tiers are optional and may be introduced in the future.** The Licensor may, but is not obliged to, introduce registration, Keys and Access Tiers in a future release of the Software, by publishing Tier Terms. Until it does so, no registration is required, the Software has no Access Tiers, every Licensee may use all functionality of the Software without registering or holding a Key, and the provisions of this License about registration, Keys, Access Tiers, Access Controls and Extra Content have no effect. Introducing Keys and Access Tiers does not reduce the functionality of releases of the Software already made without them.

Once introduced, the Software may operate at the following Access Tiers, as further described in the Tier Terms:

- **Open:** limited functionality or limited uses, without registration.
- **Friend in Good Standing:** full access, for a person who holds a valid Key and has no breach of this License that remains uncured after the cure period in Section 16.
- **Patron:** full access and any further benefits stated in the Tier Terms, for a person whose paid or supporting status is active.

A Licensee shall not:

- remove, disable, bypass, or falsify Access Controls;
- share a Key with another person, or use a Key that was not issued to that Licensee;
- distribute Software or Derivative Software in which Access Controls have been removed, disabled, or bypassed.

Modifying other parts of the Software remains permitted under Section 3.

If a breach remains uncured after the cure period in Section 16, the Licensor may suspend or revoke the Licensee's Key and reduce that Licensee to the Open tier. Doing so does not by itself terminate this License.

Extra Content is not licensed under this License. It is provided under its own terms, which remain subject to the rights of its creators under Section 15.

The Licensor may change the Tier Terms for future versions and for future periods. Changes to the Tier Terms do not reduce the access of any Friend in Good Standing to versions of the Software already released to them.

If the Licensor has introduced Keys and later permanently stops operating the Key service, the Licensor shall, no later than ninety (90) days after it stops, publish an update or other means that lets every Friend in Good Standing use the full functionality of the Software without the Key service. Where the Licensor holds the necessary rights, the Licensor shall also make the Extra Content already made available to Friends in Good Standing available for download. Apart from this, the Licensor is not obliged to continue operating any Key or online service.

## 13. Prohibited Uses

Unless expressly authorized by law, the Software may not be used primarily to create, promote, facilitate, or distribute:

- child sexual abuse material, or any sexual content involving a minor or a character or voice presented as a minor;
- human trafficking;
- non-consensual sexual content, or sexual content using the face, body, or voice of any real person without that person's consent;
- terrorist recruitment or terrorist propaganda;
- direct incitement of unlawful violence against real persons;
- fraud, scams, or criminal deception;
- content that imitates the voice or likeness of an identifiable real person without that person's prior consent (or, for a minor, the consent of a parent or legal guardian, and for a deceased person, the consent of the holder of the relevant rights) or another legal right to do so;
- impersonation of any person or organisation in order to deceive, defraud, or harass.

Nothing in this License shall prohibit lawful political speech, journalism, commentary, artistic expression, academic discussion, religious expression, satire, parody, criticism, advocacy, or public debate.

